WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.690 --> 00:00:02.755
Hello?

00:00:02.755 --> 00:00:04.480
Ooh, welcome home, honey.

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:05.290
Come take a seat.

00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:07.480
You must be starving.

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:08.600
Yeah, OK.

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:11.467
Ted, congratulations on your big win.

00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:14.050
I didn't know if you'd be in the mood for meatloaf or lasagna,

00:00:14.050 --> 00:00:14.800
so I made both.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:21.410
Mom, what's wrong?

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:23.190
Why are you here?

00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:24.020
What do you mean?

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:27.062
I mean, if you got something you need to say to me,

00:00:27.062 --> 00:00:29.270
I'd appreciate it if you just went ahead and said it.

00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:30.860
Oh, stop.

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:33.380
I just want to spend my last night in London with my son

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:37.000
and make sure everything's all right.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.570
OK.

00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:41.090
Well, thank you cooking dinner, both of them.

00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:44.218
Oh, you're welcome.

00:00:44.218 --> 00:00:46.860
[MUTED] you for not wanting to talk.

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:47.970
Excuse me?

00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:50.870
Thank you for flying all the way here to come see me.

00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:54.040
[MUTED] you for not telling me you were coming.

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:57.083
Thank you for all the small, silly little things

00:00:57.083 --> 00:00:58.500
you did for me as a kid, you know,

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:01.890
like hiding notes in my lunchbox or putting

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:04.200
googly eyes on the fruit at the supermarket

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:05.580
just to make me laugh.

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:09.510
And [MUTED] you for not working on yourself or seeking

00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:12.060
help after we lost dad and for not

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:14.190
talking to me about it either, just glossing

00:01:14.190 --> 00:01:17.820
over the whole thing and acting like everything was all right.

00:01:21.670 --> 00:01:22.945
I'm sorry.

00:01:28.070 --> 00:01:30.050
I didn't know what to do, Ted.

00:01:30.050 --> 00:01:34.280
So-- I pretended I was OK.

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:35.360
OK.

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:37.350
Well, thank you for the apology.

00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:40.340
[MUTED] you for making me think I had to pretend, too.

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:40.840
All right.

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:45.710
I appreciate you sharing all this with me.

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:48.565
I just wish you hadn't carried it around for so long.

00:01:48.565 --> 00:01:50.230
Yeah, OK.

00:01:50.230 --> 00:01:53.965
And now, you're right, Ted, I do have something to say to you.

00:01:56.780 --> 00:01:58.040
Your son misses you.

00:01:58.040 --> 00:02:01.244
[SLOW MUSIC]

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:04.178
I know.

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:08.120
I miss him, too.

00:02:17.335 --> 00:02:20.250
It's just like--

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:22.464
It's just like I'm scared.

00:02:22.464 --> 00:02:28.680
if sometimes I get close to that little boy.

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:29.300
Oh, honey.

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:29.800
Why?

00:02:34.017 --> 00:02:35.475
Because I know he's going to leave.

00:02:35.475 --> 00:02:38.640
[SLOW MUSIC]

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:44.985
Oh, well.

00:02:44.985 --> 00:02:46.300
Come on.

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:46.800
No.

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:46.980
No.

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:47.480
No.

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:49.060
No.

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:49.560
All right.

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:52.350
That is the thing about being a parent.

00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:53.910
Sometimes you lose.

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:56.490
And sometimes you win.

00:02:56.490 --> 00:02:58.020
But most of the time, you just tie.

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:04.955
All we can do is keep playing.

00:03:04.955 --> 00:03:08.264
[SLOW MUSIC]

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:15.190
Thank you.

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:19.490
[MUTED] you.

00:03:19.490 --> 00:03:21.940
[GIGGLES]

